{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.KnotEigenbasisCompleteProof","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.KnotEigenbasisCompleteProof","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CasimirShared"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.spanning","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.spanning","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L71-L71","doc":"**Spanning** (Part 3): the union of all level-`n` embedded\nsubspaces is *all* of `V_phys`.  Equivalently, every element\nof `V_phys` lies in `embed n` for some `n`.\n\nThis is the algebraic-spanning condition (no metric completion\nis invoked).  Non-vacuous: if `embed` is the constant empty\nset, this is unprovable; it captures the genuine\ndirect-limit-cover property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.embed","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The level-`n` embedded subspace: `embed n` is the image of\n`V^{⊗n}` inside `V_phys` under the direct-limit inclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.V_phys","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.V_phys","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The algebraic direct-limit type `V_phys = colim V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.summands_detected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.summands_detected","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L55-L55","doc":"For each partition `λ`, there exists a braid whose trace on the\ncorresponding Hecke-summand is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.braid_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.braid_rep","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Representation map: braid → Hecke algebra element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.consistent","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Consistency: the Markov trace is on the same Hecke algebra\nas the decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.markov","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Part 3: the Markov trace detects every irreducible summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.alexander","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.alexander","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Part 2: Alexander surjectivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.decomposition","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Part 1: the q-Schur–Weyl decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete","kind":"structure","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.lean#L20-L71","doc":"**Completeness of the knot-type eigenbasis** (Proposition 4.x).\n\nCombines semisimplicity of `H_n(q)`, Alexander surjectivity, and\nspanning of the algebraic direct limit to establish that knot types\nform a complete eigenbasis replacing the Feynman path integral.\n\nThree parts:\n1. `H_n(q)` is semisimple at generic `q`, giving the complete\n   q-Schur–Weyl decomposition of `V^{⊗n}`.\n2. Alexander's theorem provides surjectivity of the braid-closure map.\n3. The algebraic direct limit `V_phys = colim V^{⊗n}` is spanned\n   by the irreducible summands (no metric completion is used).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:knot-eigenbasis-complete","label":"prf:knot-eigenbasis-complete","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}